{'symbol': 'OMC', 'date': '2021-03-16 09:00:00', 'title': "THE NEW ESSENTIALS: A YEAR INTO THE PANDEMIC, WE AREN'T 'RETURNING' TO WORK -WE'RE REDEFINING IT", 'text': 'NEW YORK, MARCH 16, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0AFTER A YEAR OF COVID-19 AND ITS EFFECTS ON WORK, A NEW STUDY BY GLOBAL COMMUNICATIONS CONSULTANCY KETCHUM SHOWS THAT MORE THAN TWO-THIRDS (70%) OF EMPLOYED AMERICANS SAY THEY ARE MORE LIKELY TO STAY AT THEIR CURRENT JOBS THAN THEY WERE BEFORE THE PANDEMIC. BUT WITH BOTH FRONTLINE AND NON-FRONTLINE WORKERS EXPERIENCING HIGH LEVELS OF BURNOUT AS A RESULT OF THE PANDEMIC, THE STUDY REVEALS DRAMATIC SHIFTS IN WHAT PEOPLE WANT FROM THEIR EMPLOYERS.'}